{"alternate_names":[{"kind":"local","language":"fr","name":"Rhône septentrional"},{"kind":"trade","name":"Northern Rhône crus"}],"id":"place:northern-rhone","layer":"reference","name":"Northern Rhône","place_kind":"analytical_region","status":"active","summary":"An editorial and institutional grouping of the eight cru appellations between Vienne and Valence. It is not a delimited legal origin: every legal boundary in this corridor belongs to an individual appellation.","type":"place"}
{"id":"geographic_feature:rhone-river","layer":"reference","name":"Rhône (river)","status":"active","summary":"The river whose corridor organises the northern crus. It is physical geography, not a wine boundary: the bank a vineyard sits on explains orientation, never legal origin.","type":"geographic_feature"}
{"id":"geographic_feature:hermitage-hill","layer":"reference","name":"Hill of Hermitage","status":"active","summary":"The granite spur on the left bank at Tain-l'Hermitage. The hill is a landform; Hermitage AOC and Crozes-Hermitage AOC are legal areas that meet it differently.","type":"geographic_feature"}
{"id":"geographic_feature:montagne-de-crussol","layer":"reference","name":"Montagne de Crussol","status":"active","summary":"The limestone relief above Saint-Péray, left standing by secondary-era deposits over the primary granite basement.","type":"geographic_feature"}
{"id":"geographic_feature:chassis-terrace","layer":"reference","name":"Les Chassis terrace","status":"active","summary":"The lowest and most recent Quaternary terrace of southern Crozes-Hermitage, a triangle with its apex at Pont-de-l'Isère. It is a landform, not a delimited wine area.","type":"geographic_feature"}
